-e8-q leads to immediate material gain and likely decisive advantage, especially if Black cannot counter with a check or capture.\n\nReason: The pawn on e7 is one square from promotion and currently unopposed. Promoting it to a queen maximizes material gain and pressure. While other promotions (knight, bishop, rook) are possible, queen gives maximum flexibility and firepower. Delaying promotion risks allowing Black counterplay.\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e8-q'}
