16 even → dark).\n\ng8: 7+8=15 → odd → light.\n\nBut queen is on g8 — and in the initial setup, queens start on their own color: white queen on d1 — d1: 4+1=5 → odd → light. Yes, white queen on light square.\n\nSo g8 is light square.\n\ng8: light.\n\nSo queen can move diagonally to other **light squares**.\n\nLight squares: where file+rank = odd.\n\nSo from g8 (7,8), sum 15 odd → light.\n\nDiagonal moves: constant sum or difference.\n\nMain diagonal: file - rank constant.\n\nOr file + rank constant.\n\nFor same color, |Δfile| = |Δrank|.\n\nSo from g8, queen can go to:\n- f7: 6,7 → 13 odd → light → yes\n- e6: 5,6 → 11 odd → light → yes\n- d5: 4,5 → 9 odd → light → yes\n- c4: 3,4 → 7 odd → light → yes\n- b3: 2,3 → 5 odd → light → yes\n- a2: 1,2 → 3 odd → light → yes\n- Also: h7: 8,7 → 15 odd → light → yes\n\nSo Qg8 can go to a2, b3, c4, d5, e6, f7, h7 — all light-squared diagonal.\n\nAnd also orthogonally: any on g-file or 8th rank.\n\nNow, which of these attack e4?\n\ne4: file 5, rank 4 → 5+4=9 → odd → light.\n\nAttacking squares:\n- Same rank: a4 to h4\n- Same file: e1 to e8\n- Diagonals: light-squared diagonal: as above — b7, c6, d5, e4, f3, g2, h1 — yes, this is the diagonal.\n\nSo any queen on that diagonal can attack e4.\n\nFrom g8, can queen move to a square on that diagonal in one move?\n\nThat diagonal: ... d5, e4, f3, g2, h1\n\ng8 to d5: yes, as above — d5 is on the diagonal (file 4, rank 5 → 4+5=9 odd → light), and |7-4|=3, |8-5|=3 → yes, diagonal move.\n\nAnd d5 is on the same diagonal as e4: d5 to e4 is one right, one down → yes.\n\nSo **Qg8-d5** attacks e4 diagonally → **check**.\n\nSimilarly, Qg8-f7: f7 is (6,7), sum 13 odd → light, but f7 to e4: Δfile=1, Δrank=3 → not equal → not diagonal. f7 and e4 not aligned orthogonally either. So no.\n\nBut **Qg8-d5+** is a check.\n\nSimilarly, **Qg8-e6**: e6 (5,6), sum 11 odd → light. e6 to e4: same file → yes! e-file. So Qg8-e6 attacks e6, e5, e4, e3, etc. → so **attacks e4 vertically** → **check**.\n\nSo multip